WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.575
Here are the thirteen rules,
each labeled with its source.

2
00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:09.052
Most come straight from Learn: a CA with
no CRL, an endpoint that isn't HTTP,

3
00:00:09.052 --> 00:00:12.951
a CRL over the size limit
or slower than ten seconds,

4
00:00:12.951 --> 00:00:18.800
the certificate method switched off,
and CRL validation off or a CA exempted.

5
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.519
Some are the program's own design:
an early warning at eighty percent,

6
00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:27.311
a CRL nobody measured, a CA
expiring within ninety days,

7
00:00:27.311 --> 00:00:30.513
and an issuing CA missing
from the trust store.

8
00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:34.221
And two protect the strength:
PIV mapped to multifactor,

9
00:00:34.221 --> 00:00:37.180
and an enforced phishing-resistant policy.
